A||N||2||NOS3800||NOS problems got WORSE||||11||
Z||000000||NOS3800||07-22-2001||11:49 PM||||I went to the track friday nite and have developed a problem with my ZEX NOS kit. Off the line when the NOS is applied, the car sputtered and surged off the line. When the NOS was turned off it ran fine the rest of the way down the track. On the return road, I was going 20mph and punched the NOS again and it seemed fine, just no power. So I stopped. And hit the NOS again from a stop and it sputtered again.<BR>In the pits, I removed the NOS nozzle and held it while I sprayed the NOS into the air. It was CLEAR, no mist. It wasn't cold either. Whats the deal? Did I get a tank of air? Or is the pressure so low it isn't misting? I weighed the tank, and I figure I had about 4.5 pounds left in the tank. Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||11
Z||000001||Shaun41178||07-23-2001||12:24 AM||||Your tank is bunk.  Empty it and see if any of it turns foggy.  If not its crap.  Get it refilled.  You don't want air.  Try and find another place to get your bottle filled if the last place you got it was just air.  Or tell them you got a lot of air and they might cut you a break on the price of a refill.  <P>Also check your nitrous filter.  If that puppy is clogged it won't flow any nitrous and it will run like dog poo.  <P>It sounds to me like your car is running rich and that is what is making it buck cause it is way too rich off the line when no nitrous is being injected or just air is being injected.<P>Clean out filter, and get bottled filled and problem will be solved.  98% guaranteed<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||NOS3800||07-23-2001||06:50 PM||||Thanks Shaun. You and Zex both confirmed what I was hoping. That the NOS bottle is full of air. Zex said that the solenoid still functions for the fuel cause the air pressure still activates it so it was flooding the motor off the line. COOL deal cause thats a simple fix. Problem is, there are only two places around here to fill NOS tanks. The one I used and got crap, and one that closes before I get off work! I will go back and try a refund. Now I can get it filled and run my brother at Maple Grove this weekend!||||reg||7
